Read the report for construction and interpretation of duration curves and comparison of record periods. Reproduce a curve from an identified daily-flow series. Keep the chronological series alongside the sorted one: frequency alone cannot identify the length or order of droughts. Explain the assumptions needed to use a historical distribution for a future supply question.

